@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1759 = private unnamed_addr constant [599 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the absence of trailing commas.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe presence of a trailing comma can reduce diff size when parameters or\0Aelements are added or removed from function calls, function definitions,\0Aliterals, etc.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo = {\0A    \22bar\22: 1,\0A    \22baz\22: 2\0A}\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo = {\0A    \22bar\22: 1,\0A    \22baz\22: 2,\0A}\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent use of trailing commas, making the rule redundant.\0A\0A[formatter]:https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/\0A", align 1
