@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1762 = private unnamed_addr constant [506 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of trailing commas on bare (i.e., unparenthesized)\0Atuples.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe presence of a misplaced comma will cause Python to interpret the value\0Aas a tuple, which can lead to unexpected behaviour.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport json\0A\0A\0Afoo = json.dumps({\22bar\22: 1}),\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport json\0A\0A\0Afoo = json.dumps({\22bar\22: 1})\0A```\0A\0AIn the event that a tuple is intended, then use instead:\0A```python\0Aimport json\0A\0A\0Afoo = (json.dumps({\22bar\22: 1}),)\0A```\0A", align 1
