@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1836 = private unnamed_addr constant [660 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that `append`, `extend` and `remove` methods are not called on\0A`__all__`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADifferent type checkers have varying levels of support for calling these\0Amethods on `__all__`. Instead, use the `+=` operator to add items to\0A`__all__`, which is known to be supported by all major type checkers.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0A__all__ = [\22A\22, \22B\22]\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 10):\0A    __all__.append(\22C\22)\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 11):\0A    __all__.remove(\22B\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0A__all__ = [\22A\22]\0A\0Aif sys.version_info < (3, 11):\0A    __all__ += [\22B\22]\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 10):\0A    __all__ += [\22C\22]\0A```\0A", align 1
