@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1863 = private unnamed_addr constant [879 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for argument-free `@pytest.mark.<marker>()` decorators with or\0Awithout parentheses, depending on the [`lint.flake8-pytest-style.mark-parentheses`]\0Asetting.\0A\0AThe rule defaults to removing unnecessary parentheses,\0Ato match the documentation of the official pytest projects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a `@pytest.mark.<marker>()` doesn't take any arguments, the parentheses are\0Aoptional.\0A\0AEither removing those unnecessary parentheses _or_ requiring them for all\0Afixtures is fine, but it's best to be consistent.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.foo\0Adef test_something(): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.foo()\0Adef test_something(): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.mark-parentheses`\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Marks](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#marks)\0A", align 1
