@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1872 = private unnamed_addr constant [592 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for strings that include escaped quotes, and suggests changing\0Athe quote style to avoid the need to escape them.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's preferable to avoid escaped quotes in strings. By changing the\0Aouter quote style, you can avoid escaping inner quotes.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo = 'bar\\'s'\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo = \22bar's\22\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter automatically removes unnecessary escapes, making the rule\0Aredundant.\0A\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter\0A", align 1
