@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1893 = private unnamed_addr constant [2116 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for first-party imports that are only used for type annotations, but\0Aaren't defined in a type-checking block.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUnused imports add a performance overhead at runtime, and risk creating\0Aimport cycles. If an import is _only_ used in typing-only contexts, it can\0Ainstead be imported conditionally under an `if TYPE_CHECKING:` block to\0Aminimize runtime overhead.\0A\0AIf [`lint.flake8-type-checking.quote-annotations`] is set to `true`,\0Aannotations will be wrapped in quotes if doing so would enable the\0Acorresponding import to be moved into an `if TYPE_CHECKING:` block.\0A\0AIf a class _requires_ that type annotations be available at runtime (as is\0Athe case for Pydantic, SQLAlchemy, and other libraries), consider using\0Athe [`lint.flake8-type-checking.runtime-evaluated-base-classes`] and\0A[`lint.flake8-type-checking.runtime-evaluated-decorators`] settings to mark them\0Aas such.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0Aimport local_module\0A\0A\0Adef func(sized: local_module.Container) -> int:\0A    return len(sized)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0Afrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\0A\0Aif TYPE_CHECKING:\0A    import local_module\0A\0A\0Adef func(sized: local_module.Container) -> int:\0A    return len(sized)\0A```\0A\0A\0A## Preview\0AWhen [preview](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/) is enabled,\0Athe criterion for determining whether an import is first-party\0Ais stricter, which could affect whether this lint is triggered vs [`TC001`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/typing-only-third-party-import/). See [this FAQ section](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/faq/#how-does-ruff-determine-which-of-my-imports-are-first-party-third-party-etc) for more details.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-type-checking.quote-annotations`\0A- `lint.flake8-type-checking.runtime-evaluated-base-classes`\0A- `lint.flake8-type-checking.runtime-evaluated-decorators`\0A- `lint.flake8-type-checking.strict`\0A- `lint.typing-modules`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 563: Runtime annotation resolution and `TYPE_CHECKING`](https://peps.python.org/pep-0563/#runtime-annotation-resolution-and-type-checking)\0A", align 1
