@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1912 = private unnamed_addr constant [806 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for missing blank lines between methods of a class.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APEP 8 recommends exactly one blank line between methods of a class.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass MyClass(object):\0A    def func1():\0A        pass\0A    def func2():\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass MyClass(object):\0A    def func1():\0A        pass\0A\0A    def func2():\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0A## Typing stub files (`.pyi`)\0AThe typing style guide recommends to not use blank lines between methods except to group\0Athem. That's why this rule is not enabled in typing stub files.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 8: Blank Lines](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#blank-lines)\0A- [Flake 8 rule](https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E301.html)\0A- [Typing Style Guide](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/source/stubs.html#blank-lines)\0A", align 1
