@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2104 = private unnamed_addr constant [777 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `itertools.starmap` calls where the second argument is a `zip` call.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`zip`-ping iterables only to unpack them later from within `starmap` is unnecessary.\0AFor such cases, `map()` should be used instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom itertools import starmap\0A\0A\0Astarmap(func, zip(a, b))\0Astarmap(func, zip(a, b, strict=True))\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Amap(func, a, b)\0Amap(func, a, b, strict=True)  # 3.14+\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe if the `starmap` or `zip` expressions contain comments that\0Awould be deleted by applying the fix. Otherwise, the fix can be applied safely.\0A\0A## Fix availability\0A\0AThis rule will emit a diagnostic but not suggest a fix if `map` has been shadowed from its\0Abuiltin binding.\0A", align 1
